{"title":"2022 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is a multiple of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c1845fb13d048f7c9eebbe5ba1b1816e663e258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can see that the number is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the last digit is not divisible by either, according to the division rule for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This eliminates answer choices A and C.\n</p><p>For the number to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the sum of the digits must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f585533189e1ff46872bd40927159945c93f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + 9 = 2 + 9 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"15\" />, which is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This eliminates answer choice B.\n</p><p>A number is also divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if the result of subtracting the odd numbered digits from the even digits is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c4e120ae4f08e4088fe451e2c53c2a64109d178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - (1 + 9) = 1 - 10 = -9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>This is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so answer choice E is eliminated.\n</p><p>A, B, C, and E are eliminated. Thus, the only answer choice remaining is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30263042958b4e7b9b4c392b29ff267514b0994f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can remember that the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6cecbaab3e78f25b6def302a17feb06d6445771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Of these factors, the only one that is an answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30263042958b4e7b9b4c392b29ff267514b0994f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200455\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 107/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4152/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33893:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017200455 and revision id 260362. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}